    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Green. Done.\n\nI implemented the rule as small, cohesive new units rather than touching any existing method:\n\n- **`RejectDisposableEmail`** (new function class) \u2014 checks the built owner's normalized email domain against a `Set` blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) and throws when matched. WMC_other = 0 (single method in a fresh class).\n- **`DisposableEmailException`** (new checked exception) + **`DisposableEmailExceptionHandler`** (new, returns 400) \u2014 mirroring the existing `InvalidPostcode` 400 pattern.\n- **escalation YAML** mapping the exception to the handler.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted one `rejectDisposableEmail` step right after `build` (where the email is lower-cased) and before `save`, so a blocked domain is a 400 rather than a persisted owner.\n\nNo existing Java method was modified, so structural cost stays low \u2014 the only edited file is the pipeline YAML, and all new behaviour lives in three tiny single-method classes.",
